{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794520631,"nonce":"vdAqGqx4bfQ+w8RwnNbw2inZMvg=","title":"FLIP, layout and visual animations are CPU-driven and force a full paint every frame","message":"FLIP (renderer/animation/flip.rs) is evaluated on the CPU: tick_flip_animations advances each MultiKeyframeAnimation per frame, apply_flip_animation_props writes the translate into the node's render props, and the window then paints in full. has_active_flip_animations (like the visual and layout animation checks) is part of bounds_anim_active in the window's present step, which clears try_fast_paint; the compositor lists it in needs_walker and other_animations_active; animate.rs excludes it from composite promotion (\"FLIP animations re-layout under the hood, so they always need the slow path\"). So a sidebar or list that slides after a reflow walks and paints the whole visible tree each frame for the length of the slide, and the node table (122c606), which already carries motion bindings and scroll, does not reach it.\n\nFLIP is the case the node table was designed for: the node is laid out and painted once at its settled pose, and the animation is a delta from the inverted offset back to zero. The row would hold translate (dx, dy) eased to (0, 0) over the transition's duration, written as the animation plays, or later evaluated from the frame clock (P2b). Needed:\n- a producer: a flip animation names its node and its current translate as a row (as a motion binding does), instead of writing props; the walker stamps the node's primitives with its slot at the paint made at the settled pose (the paint after the reflow, with the transform at identity).\n- the fast path stays open while only flip rows change; text, SVG and images under the node move with it (rows already do for bound nodes).\n- layout and visual animations are different: an animated size or a collapse changes layout every frame, so they stay on layout and the full walk until the layout is cheap enough or the size can be a scale; do not fold them in.\n- held to the harness: the existing animation_paths scenes plus a FLIP scene (a reflow that moves a sibling), rows against a full paint.\n\nRelated: 122c606 (node table), the CSS animations and transitions on rows item in its plan, a0a05a2 (expand and collapse by layout animation).","files":null}]}